  "chapter_note": "This chapter contains essentially no cosmological substrate. It is a thoroughly Manichaean ecclesial-catechetical treatise on the salvation of catechumens — covering their post-mortem ascent, the sign/type of the perfect catechumen, the fifty Sundays of fasting, ritual purity, communion with the elect, repentance and remission of sins through the Holy Church and the Mind of Light, and reckoning of works at quarter-portions. Even cosmologically-flavored imagery (firmaments, fruits on the tree, icons of light, country of the Living Ones) is deployed in service of ecclesial doctrine about almsgiving and almsgivers. The 1 Cor 7 citation ('those who have a wife, let them be as those who have not') is embedded as apostolic authority. Editorial fatigue score is negative (-2.20) but ecclesial vocabulary is uniformly high throughout. The dialogue frame appears at the standard places (opening question, intermediate disciples' praise, closing). Damage is high (62.5%). I find no substrate worth extracting in this chapter.",
